# Chicken Tikka Masala

Based on [https://twosleevers.com/chicken-tikka-masala/](https://twosleevers.com/chicken-tikka-masala) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20260129073422/https://twosleevers.com/chicken-tikka-masala/))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Chicken Marinade

- [ ] 1.5 lbs [boneless, skinless chicken thighs]{ ing="boneless-skinless-chicken-thighs" }, cut into bite-sized pieces
- [ ] 1/2 cup [full-fat Greek yogurt]{ ing="full-fat-greek-yogurt" } (or full-fat coconut milk for dairy-free)
- [ ] 2 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, minced
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [minced ginger]{ ing="minced-ginger" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [turmeric]{ ing="turmeric" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [cayenne pepper]{ ing="cayenne-pepper" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [smoked paprika]{ ing="smoked-paprika" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [garam masala]{ ing="garam-masala" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [liquid smoke]{ ing="liquid-smoke" } (optional)

### Sauce

- [ ] 1 large [onion]{ ing="onion" }, diced
- [ ] 1 (14 oz) can [crushed tomatoes]{ ing="crushed-tomatoes" }
- [ ] 1 large [carrot]{ ing="carrot" }, peeled and diced
- [ ] 4 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, minced
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [minced ginger]{ ing="minced-ginger" }
- [ ] 2 tsp [turmeric]{ ing="turmeric" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [cayenne pepper]{ ing="cayenne-pepper" }
- [ ] 2 tsp [smoked paprika]{ ing="smoked-paprika" }
- [ ] 2 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 2 tsp [garam masala]{ ing="garam-masala" }

### Finishing

- [ ] 1/2 cup [half and half]{ ing="half-and-half" } (or coconut milk for dairy-free)
- [ ] Fresh [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }, chopped (for garnish)

### For Serving

- [ ] [Basmati rice]{ ing="basmati-rice" } or naan bread

## Recipe

1. Marinate chicken by combining chicken pieces with [yogurt]{ ing="full-fat-greek-yogurt" }, [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, [ginger]{ ing="minced-ginger" }, [turmeric]{ ing="turmeric" }, cayenne, [paprika]{ ing="smoked-paprika" }, [salt]{ ing="salt" }, [garam masala]{ ing="garam-masala" }, and [liquid smoke]{ ing="liquid-smoke" } in a bowl; mix well and set aside
1. Add all sauce ingredients ([onion]{ ing="onion" }, [tomatoes]{ ing="crushed-tomatoes" }, [carrot]{ ing="carrot" }, [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, [ginger]{ ing="minced-ginger" }, and all spices) to Instant Pot; stir to combine
1. Place marinated chicken on top of sauce (do not stir in)
1. Close Instant Pot lid and cook on high pressure for 10 minutes
1. Allow natural pressure release for 10 minutes, then release remaining pressure manually
1. Remove chicken from pot and set aside
1. Use immersion blender to blend sauce until smooth and creamy
1. Stir in [half and half]{ ing="half-and-half" } (or coconut milk)
1. Return chicken to pot and stir to coat with sauce
1. Serve over [basmati rice]{ ing="basmati-rice" } or with naan bread; garnish with fresh [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }

## Notes

- Serves 6
- Prep time: 20 minutes, Cook time: 20 minutes
- Low carb (6 net carbs per serving) and keto-compatible
- Gluten-free
- For 8-quart Instant Pots, double the recipe to avoid burn messages
- Can freeze half the sauce for future meals
- Nutrition per serving: 314 calories, 22g protein, 8g carbs
- The yogurt marinade helps tenderize the chicken and adds authentic flavor
